      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "[Followup from Sourceforge Tracker]",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Followup Submitter: sjw46",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Logged In: YES ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "user_id=1709161",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Originator: YES",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "In implementing axis error detail for authz (so that fedora-admin can say \"Not",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Authorized\" instead of \"Axis Fault\"), the existing code didn't/doesn't seem to",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "handle this correctly.  I didn't change that code.  One of us should someday",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "look at it.  ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Basically, it's that serverside error detail is input as \"<detail>line",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "one</detail><detail>line two</detail>\".  It looks like this is never parsed by",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "axis, and is just sent along as the text of a single Element built by axis. ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "This isn't grokked at the client.  I added code to actually build an Authz",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "element, for that case, which can then be grokked clientside.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
