     "body": "<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;Followup from Sourceforge Tracker&#93;</span><br/>\nFollowup Submitter: sjw46<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=1709161<br/>\nOriginator: YES</p>\n\n<p>In implementing axis error detail for authz (so that fedora-admin can say \"Not<br/>\nAuthorized\" instead of \"Axis Fault\"), the existing code didn't/doesn't seem to<br/>\nhandle this correctly.  I didn't change that code.  One of us should someday<br/>\nlook at it.  </p>\n\n<p>Basically, it's that serverside error detail is input as \"&lt;detail&gt;line<br/>\none&lt;/detail&gt;&lt;detail&gt;line two&lt;/detail&gt;\".  It looks like this is never parsed by<br/>\naxis, and is just sent along as the text of a single Element built by axis. <br/>\nThis isn't grokked at the client.  I added code to actually build an Authz<br/>\nelement, for that case, which can then be grokked clientside.</p>",
     "created": "12/Mar/07 5:19 PM",
